T H E  T W O  G R A N D  T H E O R I E S
When humankind began to think in depth about itself, it developed beliefs
to m ake ö chaos. These master creeds tend to split into two
contradictory po ints ż on  why š do the things they do.
They tak e either  the inside-out subjective, intrinsic view ¤  self, or the
outside-in objective, extrinsic angle of society . In other words, nature ³
