T wenty-First Century
ë most rece nt decades, the polarized dialogue on human nature took
this form:
Extrinsic
Critical Theory , aka postmodern ism, is a nurture-based system that sees the
mind as  a socially conditioned or gan. Therefore, the use of one culture’ s
subjective belief s to judge another culture’ s behaviors and values is bigoted.
This co nviction went so far a s to reject the scientific method itself—
