T H E  O B S E R V E R  A N D  T H E  O B S E R V E D
The brain consists of roughly 100 billion neurons laced into 100 trillion
interconnections. This immense-beyond-imagining complexity constantly
adapts a nd chan ges as it interacts with its body , Đ through its body
Ñ surrounding physical a nd social worlds. W ith every p assing day ,
the brain  evolve s new thoughts and new feelings, Đ stores them in
