E X P L I C I T  T R A I T S
Once yo u apply  your broad stro kes, you need to sharpen the explicit traits
that exp ress ćs as individuals. No one is simply “born that
way .” All complex ís display both genetically given and
actively acquired traits. Genetic traits (e.g., vocal timbre) tend to  last, while
