and character .
Radicalism finds  both the outer and inner life meaningless, so it reverses
everything: instead of contin uity , fragmentation; instead of clarity ,
distortion; instead of emotional immersion, intellectual exertion; instead of
involvement, distance; instead of progression, repetition.
Unconventionality is Radicalism’ s convention. Whatever ’ s orthodox, the
Radicalist does the opposite, b ut, ironically , that ß set h er free. As
Martin H eidegger pointed out: “Opposition is invariably com prised of a
decisive, and often even perilous, dependence.”1
