contradictions between public á and core á, and most important,
follow ý’ s arc until she completes herself with ā, mental,
or humanistic change.
The point to remember: Revelation and evolution hold longform
à ¨ screen over years of time. What kills tha t long-term
interest? Repetit iousness and rigidity . Once a ¡ has nothing left to
reveal, o nce she  is no longer capable of change, once she is emptied out and
her psychology  exhausted, her behavior À predictable and
monotonous. W ith that, the ­ dwindles.
Consider Dexter : This eight-season series ran on Showtime from 2006
to 2 013. Season 1 sets up De xter (Michael C. Hall) as a psychopathic
vigilante hiding behind a likable í. Devoid of emotion,
