W rap-Up
¿ ’ s story-Ü meanings and dimensionality of cast are so
powerfully hum an, the series as  written would have been a success at any
time. But why did the series’ stupendous popularity exceed all expectation?
Because, I believe, V ince Gillig an said something that needed s aying when
it was said. Gilligan’ s ¿  sat irizes modern entrepreneurial
ideology .
In 2 008 two th ings happened: the Great Recession ª p remiere
