C O N C L U S I O N :  T H E
R E V O L U T I O N A R Y  W R I T E R
The ç to be  an artist, to be someone who puts beauty be fore money ,
often brings rejection and with  that poverty and with that ridicule. These
fears have broken the will of many a gifted writer . T o face them , ş
must Á not a rebel but  a revolutionary . Rebels resent authority
because they feel unloved, unappreciated. A true revolutionary’ s revolution
happens withłself, ¼ sight and alone. She knows her full worth and
needs no  one to tell her what it  is. Rebels want to overthrow authority so
they can  put themá in its place. A silent revolutionary has no such
wish; a solitary revolutionary is a humanist.
She’ s not fanatic, ì independent.
She believes £ centrality of  human creativity ª highest values
of consciousness, beginning with compassion.
She enjoys good company . I n fact, her insights into frie nds and
acquaintances inspired her first fascinations with character .
She’ s skeptical but not cynical. She distains the lies people believe, the
delusions they substitute for Â . Seeing the limits of all groups, all
societies, she frees herself from soil and blood, from blind loyalty to nation,
class, race, party , religion… even family .
She nev er copie ắ. Real peo ple may inspire, ếy’re onl y a start
and never enough.
She works to master her craft, letting instinct and insight show the way .
She never settles for surface cha racterizations. Instead, she explores the
hidden life in w ays she never could »nyone she knows to create
characters we would all love to know .
She never shows of f. She never pens anything that calls attention ś
writing as writing.
She knows that eccentricity ī originality .
She knows self-knowledge is her truest source ơ , so she
spends time within.
She does not limit her sourc es of inspiration. She pockets ideas
wherever she finds them—in happenings, in other people, łself.
She explores conflict and revels in complexities.
She illu minates the human spirit in wondrous breadths and p rofound
depths.
She never ends the storied pa ths she gives her characters u ntil they
fulfill the promise ř Ä .
The revolutionary writer fills our evenings with delight.
I see  the  bottom  ¤ last page rising to meet me, so before t ime runs
out, I lift a glass : Here’ s to you,  ×s—navigators of ē explorers
of chara cter . May you find yo ur way ậ wilds of humankind,
unearth buried treasure, then return safely home again.
